<rml>
<head>
	<title>Main Frame</title>
	<link type="text/rcss" href="base.rcss"/>
	<link type="text/rcss" href="main_frame.rcss"/>
</head>
<body data-model="main_frame">
	<!-- Modern theme's own copy of CNewUIMainFrameWindow's HP/MP/AG/SD/EXP bars + 5 corner
	     buttons (Phase 1 of 3 of the CNewUIObj-tier pilot; skill list / item hotkeys are out of
	     scope, still fully legacy-rendered). Per-theme file (UI::RmlBridge::LoadThemedDocument)
	     because the bottom-HUD button row is genuinely absent here (moved to #top_right_row
	     below), not just hidden via CSS -- CSS-only hiding proved unreliable for this element, and
	     a C++ theme-awareness flag was tried and rejected as inconsistent with this branch's
	     "theme differences live in theme files" principle. Keep this file's ids/classes/bindings
	     in sync with themes/legacy/main_frame.rml except #buttons/#buttons_top. #bars binds
	     left/top/scale live from C++ (tracks the still-legacy center-band chrome's own scale);
	     #exp nests inside #bars to inherit that transform, using plain reference-pixel
	     coordinates. -->
	<div id="bars" data-style-left="bars_left + 'px'" data-style-top="bars_top + 'px'" data-style-transform="'scale(' + bars_scale + ')'">
		<!-- Read-only-from-C++ anchors marking where the still-legacy item-hotkey/skill-hotkey
		     bands should be positioned -- lets each theme control that legacy content's anchor
		     without C++ knowing which theme is active. -->
		<div id="item_hotkey_anchor" class="layout-anchor"></div>
		<div id="skill_list_anchor" class="layout-anchor"></div>
		<!-- #gauge_frame (the continuous top border) is deliberately declared AFTER the two fill
		     divs, not before -- same-stacking-level siblings paint in DOM order, and
		     #gauge_fill_left/right's own solid background otherwise paints over #gauge_frame's
		     thin top border wherever the two overlap (the left/right zones), leaving the border
		     visible only in the middle where nothing else paints on top of it. -->
		<div id="gauge_fill_left"></div>
		<div id="gauge_fill_right"></div>
		<div id="gauge_frame"></div>
		<div id="bar_hp" class="gauge-slot slot-frame slot-fill">
			<div id="bar_hp_fill" class="gauge-fill gauge-fill-hp gauge-fill-vertical" data-class-poisoned="poisoned" data-style-height="hp_fraction * 100 + '%'"></div>
			<div class="gauge-fill gauge-fill-hp gauge-fill-horizontal" data-class-poisoned="poisoned" data-style-width="hp_fraction * 100 + '%'"></div>
			<span class="gauge-num">{{hp_text}}</span>
		</div>
		<span class="tooltip tooltip-hp">{{hp_tooltip}}</span>
		<div id="bar_sd" class="gauge-slot slot-frame slot-fill">
			<div class="gauge-fill gauge-fill-sd gauge-fill-vertical" data-style-height="sd_fraction * 100 + '%'"></div>
			<div class="gauge-fill gauge-fill-sd gauge-fill-horizontal" data-style-width="sd_fraction * 100 + '%'"></div>
			<span class="gauge-num">{{sd_text}}</span>
		</div>
		<span class="tooltip tooltip-sd">{{sd_tooltip}}</span>
		<div id="bar_ag" class="gauge-slot slot-frame slot-fill">
			<div class="gauge-fill gauge-fill-ag gauge-fill-vertical" data-style-height="ag_fraction * 100 + '%'"></div>
			<div class="gauge-fill gauge-fill-ag gauge-fill-horizontal" data-style-width="ag_fraction * 100 + '%'"></div>
			<span class="gauge-num">{{ag_text}}</span>
		</div>
		<span class="tooltip tooltip-ag">{{ag_tooltip}}</span>
		<div id="bar_mp" class="gauge-slot slot-frame slot-fill">
			<div class="gauge-fill gauge-fill-mp gauge-fill-vertical" data-style-height="mp_fraction * 100 + '%'"></div>
			<div class="gauge-fill gauge-fill-mp gauge-fill-horizontal" data-style-width="mp_fraction * 100 + '%'"></div>
			<span class="gauge-num">{{mp_text}}</span>
		</div>
		<span class="tooltip tooltip-mp">{{mp_tooltip}}</span>

		<!-- EXP: spans this group's own reference width (item-hotkey band's start to button
		     group's end). exp_fraction is progress within the current decile, not overall level. -->
		<div id="exp">
			<div id="exp_track" class="slot-frame slot-fill">
				<div id="exp_fill" data-style-width="exp_fraction * 100 + '%'"></div>
			</div>
			<span id="exp_digit">{{exp_digit}}</span>
			<span class="tooltip" id="exp_tooltip">{{exp_tooltip}}</span>
		</div>

		<!-- Decorative slot outlines for the still-legacy item-hotkey/skill icons -- legacy hides
		     these outright, its own sprite chrome already frames the slots. -->
		<div id="item_slots">
			<div id="item_slot_0" class="slot-frame"><span class="slot-hotkey-label">Q</span></div>
			<div id="item_slot_1" class="slot-frame"><span class="slot-hotkey-label">W</span></div>
			<div id="item_slot_2" class="slot-frame"><span class="slot-hotkey-label">E</span></div>
			<div id="item_slot_3" class="slot-frame"><span class="slot-hotkey-label">R</span></div>
		</div>
		<!-- data-class-selected mirrors which hotkey slot currently shows the equipped skill.
		     skill-hotkey-label shows the assigned hotkey number -- own class, not
		     .slot-hotkey-label (the potion Q/W/E/R labels' class), since legacy wants this one
		     genuinely visible (own real content, not baked into any sprite) where it hides the
		     other. Empty string -> nothing rendered, for an unbound slot. -->
		<div id="skill_slots">
			<div id="skill_slot_0" class="slot-frame" data-class-selected="skill_slot_0_selected"><span class="skill-hotkey-label">{{skill_slot_0_hotkey}}</span></div>
			<div id="skill_slot_1" class="slot-frame" data-class-selected="skill_slot_1_selected"><span class="skill-hotkey-label">{{skill_slot_1_hotkey}}</span></div>
			<div id="skill_slot_2" class="slot-frame" data-class-selected="skill_slot_2_selected"><span class="skill-hotkey-label">{{skill_slot_2_hotkey}}</span></div>
			<div id="skill_slot_3" class="slot-frame" data-class-selected="skill_slot_3_selected"><span class="skill-hotkey-label">{{skill_slot_3_hotkey}}</span></div>
			<div id="skill_slot_4" class="slot-frame" data-class-selected="skill_slot_4_selected"><span class="skill-hotkey-label">{{skill_slot_4_hotkey}}</span></div>
			<div id="current_skill_slot" class="slot-frame"></div>
		</div>
	</div>

	<!-- Top-right system-button panel -- moved here from the bottom HUD, visually echoing
	     mu_helper_bar's own panel styling for a cohesive top-HUD feel. Its own sibling document
	     element, not merged into mu_helper_bar.rml (separate C++ owners/data models; RmlUi
	     documents can't share a real DOM parent across document boundaries anyway).
	     #top_right_row positions itself via `display:flex; justify-content:flex-end` rather than
	     `.anchor-top-right`'s `right:0` -- `right` was confirmed (isolation test) not to render
	     this element at all in this document, root cause never found; flex sidesteps the bug. -->
	<div id="top_right_row" class="anchor-top-left">
		<div id="buttons_top">
			<div id="btn_cshop_top" class="frame-btn-top" data-class-open="cshop_open" data-event-click="mainframe_cshop_click">
				<span>SHOP</span>
			</div>
			<span class="tooltip-top" id="tooltip_cshop_top">{{cshop_tooltip}}</span>
			<div id="btn_chainfo_top" class="frame-btn-top" data-class-open="chainfo_open" data-event-click="mainframe_chainfo_click">
				<span>CHAR</span>
				<div class="alert-dot-top" data-class-hidden="!chainfo_alert"></div>
			</div>
			<span class="tooltip-top" id="tooltip_chainfo_top">{{chainfo_tooltip}}</span>
			<div id="btn_myinven_top" class="frame-btn-top" data-class-open="myinven_open" data-event-click="mainframe_myinven_click">
				<span>INV</span>
			</div>
			<span class="tooltip-top" id="tooltip_myinven_top">{{myinven_tooltip}}</span>
			<div id="btn_friend_top" class="frame-btn-top" data-class-open="friend_open" data-event-click="mainframe_friend_click">
				<span>FRIEND</span>
				<div class="alert-dot-top" data-class-hidden="!friend_alert"></div>
			</div>
			<span class="tooltip-top" id="tooltip_friend_top">{{friend_tooltip}}</span>
			<div id="btn_window_top" class="frame-btn-top" data-class-open="window_open" data-event-click="mainframe_window_click">
				<span>MENU</span>
			</div>
			<span class="tooltip-top" id="tooltip_window_top">{{window_tooltip}}</span>
		</div>
	</div>
</body>
</rml>
